mission "The Fleet at the Blue Line"
    name "The Fleet at the Blue Line"
    description "Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal."
    source "Pelican's Rest"
    destination "Stormhaven"
    reward 1590
    speaker offer "Admiral Horatio Vale"
    speaker visit "Admiral Horatio Vale"
    speaker complete "Admiral Horatio Vale"
    to offer
        has "The Drowned Crown Coordinates: done"
    objective kills 2
    battlefield "The Blue Line" 14597.8 5501.5
    enemy "Vale's Vanguard"
    enemy "Vale's Second"
    on offer
        conversation
            `The survey ships are taking their lantern stations along the blue line. Their code marks safe water, but another squadron has mistaken it for a signal to a treasure fleet.`
            `Admiral Horatio Vale watches the approaching sails. "If those ships reach the survey vessels before we explain the code, they will fire first and ask questions after. I need you between them long enough for the captains to understand."`
            choice
                `"All right. Put me on the course."`
                    accept
                `"Why has someone gone to such trouble to hide this?"`
                    goto details
                `"My ship has enough trouble without this. I will pass."`
                    close
            label details
                `Vale points to the survey line. "Keep our ships together and drive the attackers off. Do not let a false signal turn this passage into a battle neither side intended."`
                choice
                    `"Mark the course. My ship is ready."`
                        accept
                    `"Not this voyage. Find another ship."`
                        close
    on accept
        log "Accepted The Fleet at the Blue Line. Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal."
    on visit
        conversation
            `At Stormhaven, Vale reviews the lantern reports. The attackers mistook the survey signal for a treasure marker, and the survey ships are safe. "A few lamps nearly cost us a fleet," he says. "We must be clearer next time."`
    on complete
        conversation
            `Vale dismisses the signalmen and turns to you. "The survey ships are safe, and the captains have corrected their signal book. You have saved more than timber and canvas today; you have kept a misunderstanding from becoming a war."`
        log "Completed The Fleet at the Blue Line. Received 1590 gold. Protect the survey ships from a squadron that has mistaken their lantern code for a treasure signal."
